# TraceWeave-Core
#
# The data root lives OUTSIDE this repo at ~/traceweave-data (see MANIFEST.md §1.1:
# Docker Desktop cannot bind-mount /tmp, so corpus paths must be under $HOME).
# These rules apply if you choose to bring parts of it in-tree.

# --- regenerable corpus scratch: never commit -------------------------------
# refrepos/ is 250 MB of shallow clones, rebuildable from
#   traceweave/config/reference_repos.txt
refrepos/
work/
traces/
*.parquet

# --- DO commit corpus provenance --------------------------------------------
# corpus/ (or traceweave-data/out) holds result.env + lock.txt + attempt.log.
# ~4 MB at 450 candidates, and it CANNOT be regenerated: lock.txt records what
# PyPI resolved on a specific date, and re-resolving changes lock_sha256 and
# therefore the repo's identity 5-tuple. See MIGRATION.md §1.
# Deliberately NOT ignored. Do not add corpus/ here.

# --- python -----------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
.mypy_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# --- editors / os -----------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store

# --- secrets ----------------------------------------------------------------
# github_meta.py reads GITHUB_TOKEN from the environment; never from a file.
.env
*.token

# --- claude code local settings (machine-specific, not shared) --------------
.claude/
.gstack/

# Written by traceweave/static/build_image.sh, and specific to the machine that
# ran it (image id, platform, the node version Debian happened to supply). The
# authoritative copy is not this file: extract.py stamps it into every repo's
# ledger record, so each S carries the provenance of the image that produced it.
# Committing it would just churn between the manager and execution hosts.
traceweave/static/image_provenance.json
